title A trip in their box
intro Blue is attacking, close to Red's goal.
flip vertical

setup
  lineup 7v7
  player B-LF at 92, 28
  player R-CB at 92, 36
  ball with B-LF

step
  caption Blue is inside Red's big box, going for a shot.
  draw penalty-area right

step
  caption A Red player sticks out a leg and trips Blue over.
  R-CB to 92, 31
  B-LF to 89, 33
  label R-CB Trip
  arrow from R-CB to B-LF
  banner Foul
  draw penalty-area right
  draw penalty-spot right
  duration 1100

question
  prompt Is that allowed?
  answer No
  wrong Yes
  wrong Yes, if you reach the ball first
  wrong Only outside the box
  correct That is a foul.
  why You cannot stick out a leg and trip someone. Go for the ball, not the player.

question
  prompt What does Blue get?
  answer A penalty kick
  wrong A free kick
  wrong A corner
  wrong A throw-in
  correct A penalty kick.
  why A foul inside the box is a penalty kick — one Blue player against the goalie.

question
  prompt Where is it kicked from?
  answer The penalty spot
  wrong The corner
  wrong The halfway line
  wrong The center circle
  correct The penalty spot.
  why Every penalty kick is taken from the little spot in front of the goal.
